--
N5008 [class.base.init]/1,/6 + [temp.variadic]/5,8: std::pair's
out-of-line DELEGATING piecewise constructor, whose delegation target has
four zipped packs (two type, two non-type index packs).  Was KNOWNBUG;
fixed by a chain of five front-end changes: (1) non-type pack values
recorded/replayed in the multi-pack #deduced_packs machinery; (2) the
out-of-line definition attach/merge sites copy the ctor-initializer along
with the body ([class.base.init]/1: the ctor-initializer is part of the
definition); (3) same-named overloaded member-template definitions are
discriminated by parameter count ([over.load]); (4) empty-pack
mem-initializer argument removal keeps sizeof... mentions
([temp.variadic]/8) while dropping genuine expansions ([temp.variadic]/4);
(5) the drain replays persisted #fn_template_packs so multi-pack members
convert with the correct pack split.  g++/clang++ runtime-verified.
